.TH PSYCHE 1 psyche\-VERSION
.SH NAME
psyche \- minimalist Xray TUN VPN client for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B psyche
.RB [ \-u
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR dev ]
.RB [ \-\-fp
.IR profile ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B psyche
is a minimalist terminal user interface VPN client for Linux that orchestrates
Xray-core in TUN mode. Designed with a minimalist philosophy, it operates with zero
graphical toolkit dependencies (using raw termios), automatically inherits terminal
emulator color schemes, and provides full system-wide Layer 3 routing.
.P
On first launch without configuration, a minimal setup window prompts for a
subscription URL. Once validated, nodes are cached locally and the main navigator
launches.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-u " url" ", \-\-url " url
Fetch and load subscription nodes from the specified URL.
.TP
.BI \-f " file" ", \-\-file " file
Load subscription nodes from a local text file.
.TP
.BI \-d " dev" ", \-\-dev " dev
Override the default TUN interface name (default configured in config.h, usually
.BR psyche0 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-fp " profile"
Set the initial uTLS fingerprint profile (e.g.
.BR chrome ,
.BR randomized ,
.BR firefox ,
.BR safari ,
.BR ios ).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Enter
Connect to the selected node, or disconnect if already connected to it.
.TP
.B j, Down
Move selection down.
.TP
.B k, Up
Move selection up.
.TP
.B g
Jump to the top of the node list.
.TP
.B G
Jump to the bottom of the node list.
.TP
.B d
Disconnect the active VPN tunnel.
.TP
.B f
Cycle TLS/uTLS fingerprint profile. Relinks the active tunnel if connected.
.TP
.B p
Perform a TCP ping latency probe against the selected node.
.TP
.B P
Perform a parallel non-blocking TCP ping latency probe against all filtered nodes.
.TP
.B o
Sort nodes by latency (toggles ascending / descending / original subscription order).
.TP
.B /
Enter search/filter mode. Press Escape to clear filter.
.TP
.B s
Enter or change the subscription URL.
.TP
.B u
Update nodes by re-fetching the configured subscription URL.
.TP
.B q
Disconnect and quit cleanly.
.SH PRIVACY AND LEAK MITIGATION
.B psyche
incorporates kernel-level protections:
.IP \(bu 2
Parent Death Signal (\fBPR_SET_PDEATHSIG\fR): Ensures the child Xray process is
instantly terminated if Psyche exits or terminates unexpectedly.
.IP \(bu 2
IPv6 Shielding: Temporarily disables IPv6 on all interfaces during an active link
to eliminate dual-stack address leaks.
.IP \(bu 2
Safe Routing: Routes traffic via \fB0.0.0.0/1\fR and \fB128.0.0.0/1\fR to prevent
routing loops and preserve original gateway interfaces.
.IP \(bu 2
Direct Kernel Netlink: Uses in-process \fBAF_NETLINK\fR sockets to manipulate links and routes without spawning external processes.
.IP \(bu 2
Atomic DNS: Employs atomic \fBrename(2)\fR operations on the same filesystem with symlink resolution to prevent corrupting \fB/etc/resolv.conf\fR.
.SH PRIVILEGES AND CAPABILITIES
.B psyche
supports running with Linux ambient file capabilities:
.PP
.nf
    sudo setcap cap_net_admin,cap_net_bind_service+ep /usr/local/bin/psyche
.fi
.PP
When set, \fBpsyche\fR runs completely unprivileged without needing \fBsudo\fR or \fBdoas\fR. When started via \fBsudo\fR, \fBpsyche\fR drops effective privileges to the caller's real user ID (\fBSUDO_UID\fR) during the interactive session.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/psyche/config.json
Application configuration (subscription URL, interface name, fingerprint).
.TP
.I ~/.config/psyche/cached_nodes.txt
Offline cache of subscription nodes.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
.B psyche
is configured at compile time through
.I config.h
(copied from
.IR config.def.h ).
Edit this file to alter default ports, interface names, and visual parameters.
